%N A399322 Number of transmission irregular trees with n unlabeled vertices.
%C A399322 The vertex transmission of a vertex in a connected graph is the sum of the distances from that vertex to all the other vertices. A connected graph is transmission irregular if every vertex has a distinct vertex transmission.
%C A399322 In this list, the trivial tree is considered transmission irregular.
%D A399322 I. Stošić and I. Damnjanović, An efficient algorithm for generating transmission irregular trees, Comput. Appl. Math. 45 (2026), Art. No. 80.
%H A399322 I. Stošić and I. Damnjanović, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.15453">An efficient algorithm for generating transmission irregular trees</a>, arXiv:2502.15453 [cs.DM], 2025.
%H A399322 I. Stošić and I. Damnjanović, <a href="https://gitlab.com/ivan100sic/trees-transmission">An efficient algorithm for generating transmission irregular trees: Supplementary material (GitLab repository)</a>.
%H A399322 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/VertexTransmission.html">Vertex Transmission</a>.
%e A399322 The only transmission irregular tree on 7 vertices is the starlike tree with a central vertex of degree three and three pendent paths of lengths 1, 2 and 3.
